/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E (The system's structural design, or class diagram, is illustrated in figure 4. While the Session class handles session parameters like session ID and expiration, the User class contains important user data including username, email, hashed password, and 2FA settings. The authService class serves as the entry point for the authentication procedure and offers methods for user signup, login, and logout. Session token creation, validation, and revocation are managed by the TokenManager. The Component class handles data-related functions, such as storing user data, retrieving logs, and saving logs. User input handling and output display fall under the control of the UI Component class.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [6]
>>
